# --- Local `npm run dev` (recommended) ---
# Leave VITE_BACKEND_HTTP and VITE_BACKEND_WS **unset** so the browser talks to Vite (5173) and Vite
# proxies /api + /ws to the backend. Proxy target = backend/.env PORT (default 8000), or override:
# VITE_DEV_API_PORT=8020
# VITE_DEV_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8020
# If your shell exports PORT=8020 for the backend, Vite inherits it and the proxy uses it automatically.
# Or set BACKEND_PORT=8020 when PORT is used for something else.
#
# If you set VITE_BACKEND_HTTP, the browser calls the API **directly** (bypasses Vite). It must match
# backend PORT exactly or login will show "Failed to fetch". CORS must allow http://localhost:5173.
# VITE_BACKEND_HTTP=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# VITE_BACKEND_WS=ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws
#
# Production Docker / same host: leave unset so the build uses same-origin /api (see Dockerfile ENV).

# Chart: how often to call `/api/market/candles` as a REST backstop (main pair still updates from WS `market`).
# Default 15000 ms if unset; clamped 5000–120000 at runtime.
# VITE_CHART_REST_RECONCILE_MS=15000

